WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.840
SCP-682 Vs SCP-101.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:08.000
Could the Hungry Bag finally be the anomaly
that doesn’t find the Hard to Destroy Reptile

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.360
too tough to swallow?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:15.520
SCP-101, the Hungry Bag, is a small, tooth-lined
bag seemingly connected to a limitless pocket

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.480
dimension, capable of devouring almost anything.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:24.320
Dr. Lee Roy Carlson suggested it might be
perfect to finish off 682 after it was reduced

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.080
in size by another anomaly.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:29.520
So after SCP-682 was shrunk&nbsp;
down by a confrontation&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.680
with SCP-165-1, its tiny body was thrown into

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.280
the gaping maw of SCP-101, and swallowed up.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:41.760
Later, however, SCP-101 began to gurgle for
an extended period.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.760
After a prolonged period of discomfort, it
belched up the tiny SCP-682, which later returned

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.200
to its normal size.

